>e

At Witt's End
You are at Witt's End. Passages lead off in *all* directions.

>drop magazines
You really are at wit's end.

[The score has just gone up by one point.]

>go to complex junction

At Complex Junction
You are at a complex junction. A low hands and knees passage from the north joins a higher crawl from the east to make a walking passage going west. There is also a large room above. The air is damp here.

>n

Shell Room
You're in a large room carved out of sedimentary rock. The floor and walls are littered with bits of shells imbedded in the stone. A shallow passage proceeds downward, and a somewhat steeper one leads up. A low hands and knees passage enters from the south.
There is an enormous clam here with its shell tightly closed.

>open clam with trident
A glistening pearl falls out of the clam and rolls away. Goodness, this must really be an oyster. (I never was very good at identifying bivalves.) Whatever it is, it has now snapped shut again.

>d

Ragged Corridor
You are in a long sloping corridor with ragged sharp walls.

>d

Cul-de-Sac
You are in a cul-de-sac about eight feet across.

Off to one side lies a glistening pearl!

>take pearl
Taken!

A sepulchral voice reverberating through the cave says, "Cave closing soon. All adventurers exit immediately through main office."

[The score has just gone up by thirty-two points.]

>go to inside

Inside Building
You are inside a building, a well house for a large spring.
A solid golden chain lies in coils on the ground!
The Persian rug is spread out on the floor here.

You can also see a selection of rare spices, a large gold nugget, some precious jewelry, some bars of silver, many rare coins, some diamonds and a treasure chest here.

>off
You switch the brass lantern off.

>drop pillow
Dropped.

>drop all but lamp
glistening pearl: Safely deposited.
ming vase: (coming to rest, delicately, on the velvet pillow)
Safely deposited.
platinum pyramid: Safely deposited.
jeweled trident: Safely deposited.
emerald the size of a plover's egg: Safely deposited.

[The score has just gone up by forty-five points.]

